<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21236] OBD_FREE_LARGE() can sleep under a spinlock, causing soft lockups</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21236</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Since &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18687" title="Separate userspace/compat code from kernel code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18687"&gt;LU-18687&lt;/a&gt; (2.17.0), OBD_FREE_LARGE() frees vmalloc memory with vfree(), which can sleep, and some callers hold a spinlock: ptlrpc_server_drop_request() frees request buffers under scp_lock. On kernels without CONFIG_PREEMPT_COUNT, such as RHEL 8, the holder can be scheduled out while the other service threads on its CPT spin on the lock:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;ptlrpc_main -&amp;gt; ptlrpc_server_drop_request -&amp;gt; queued_spin_lock_slowpath
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With PREEMPT_COUNT this is only a debug kernel warning (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19869" title="BUG: sleeping function called from invalid context at mm/vmalloc.c" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19869"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19869&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fixed one caller). OBD_FREE_LARGE() can defer the free whenever preemptible() is false, which fixes every caller at once.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
        <key id="100493">LU-21236</key>
            <summary>OBD_FREE_LARGE() can sleep under a spinlock, causing soft lockups</summary>
